return [
    '/filing-storage/' => 'Filing and storage is the backbone of any well-run Nigerian office, school or government registry, and it is where paperwork either stays findable or quietly disappears. This section brings together everything you need to capture, organise and archive documents: archive boxes for long-term storage, desk filing to keep active paperwork within reach, and a full range of files and folders for day-to-day use. Whether you are kitting out a records room in Lagos, standardising a departmental registry or restocking a busy front office, the goal is the same, a system that holds up to constant handling and lets staff retrieve any file in seconds. When choosing, think in terms of the whole workflow rather than single items: how documents arrive, where live files sit, and how closed files are boxed and stored. Match capacities and sizes across products so folders, binders and boxes work together instead of against each other, and plan for Nigeria\'s humidity, which can warp card and encourage mould over the years. OfficeLand stocks dependable filing and storage from trusted names including Bantex and Leitz, supplied to offices, schools and public-sector registries nationwide. Explore the subcategories below to build a complete filing setup, and request a quote for bulk or recurring supply, answered within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/archive-boxes/' => 'Archive boxes are built for the documents you must keep but rarely touch, closed case files, prior-year accounts, personnel records and statutory paperwork that has to survive long after it leaves the active desk. The right box protects its contents for years, so look first at board strength and construction: a rigid, double-walled box with reinforced corners will stack several high without crushing the ones beneath, which matters in a crowded Lagos store room or basement registry. Check the internal dimensions against what you actually file, whether that is foolscap folders, lever arch files laid flat or loose correspondence, and make sure the lid fits snugly to keep dust out. Clear labelling panels and secure hand-holes speed up both storage and retrieval when boxes are shelved in rows. Nigeria\'s humidity is the real enemy of long-term archives, so store boxes off the floor, away from damp walls, and choose sturdier board where conditions are difficult. For large clear-outs and annual archiving, buying in volume keeps your box sizes consistent and your shelving uniform. OfficeLand supplies archive and storage boxes in practical sizes for offices, schools and government registries across Nigeria. Tell us your quantities and we will send a quote within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/desk-filing/' => 'Desk filing is about the paperwork in motion, the letters, forms, invoices and memos that pass across a desk each day and need somewhere orderly to rest between tasks. Good desk filing keeps active documents sorted and visible without letting them sprawl, and it is the difference between a front desk that runs smoothly and one buried under loose sheets. This section covers the items that organise your working surface, including document trays for incoming, outgoing and in-progress paperwork, and magazine holders that stand reports, catalogues and bound documents upright and easy to pull. When selecting, think about how your team processes work, how many stages a document moves through, how much space each desk allows, and whether pieces should stack or sit side by side. Durability counts too, since these items are handled constantly throughout the working day. For a shared registry, reception or open-plan office, choosing a consistent style and colour across every desk makes the whole space look organised and keeps restocking simple. OfficeLand offers desk filing suited to Nigerian offices, schools and public-sector workspaces, with nationwide delivery and bulk supply. Browse the options below and request a quote, answered within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/desk-filing/document-trays/' => 'Document trays, often searched for as letter trays or in-out trays, are the simplest way to bring order to a busy desk. They separate incoming post from work in progress and items ready to go out, so nothing is missed and nothing is handled twice. The practical decisions are about material and stacking: wire mesh trays are light and let you see contents at a glance, while moulded trays feel more solid and sit flat on the desk. Look at how they stack, risers and interlocking designs let you build vertical tiers to save surface space, which is useful at a cramped reception or in a shared Lagos office where desks are close together. Check that the tray takes your standard paper size comfortably, whether A4 or foolscap, so sheets do not curl over the edges. For a registry or a row of clerical desks, matching trays across every workstation keeps the office looking tidy and makes reordering straightforward. OfficeLand supplies document and letter trays in single units and stackable sets for offices, schools and government departments throughout Nigeria. Let us know how many desks you are fitting out and we will prepare a quote within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/desk-filing/magazine-holders/' => 'Magazine holders, also called magazine files or magazine racks, stand upright on a shelf or desk to keep bound material tidy and easy to reach. They are ideal for catalogues, journals, training manuals, bound reports and the thin files that slump and scatter when laid flat. When choosing, weigh the material against the wear it will take: sturdy board holders are economical and work well for lighter use, while rigid plastic or metal versions stand up to years of handling in a busy registry or library. Consider the open front and spine design, a cut-away front lets staff read titles and pull items quickly, while a full spine offers more support for heavier contents. A clear label area on the spine makes a shelf of holders easy to scan and keeps sequences in order. Line several along a shelf and you have an instant, space-saving reference section for an office, school library or departmental resource room. OfficeLand stocks magazine holders in a range of styles and finishes, supplied in bulk to organisations across Nigeria with nationwide delivery. Request a quote for your quantities and we will respond within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/' => 'Files and folders are the everyday workhorses of document management, and this section gathers the full range an office, school or registry relies on. From lightweight manila folders that hold a single matter to robust lever arch files and ring binders that carry whole projects, the right folder depends entirely on how the document will be used, stored and retrieved. As an overview, think about three things when planning your filing: capacity, how many sheets each file must hold; compatibility, whether contents sit loose, on prongs, in rings or in suspension; and durability, since files that are opened daily in a heavy registry wear out far faster than those that are filed and left. The subcategories below break this down, covering display books and clear files for presentation, dividers and index sets for navigation, document files and boxes, lever arch files, manila folders, report and clip files, ring binders and suspension files. Standardising on a few file types across departments keeps your filing cabinets consistent and reordering simple. OfficeLand carries trusted brands including Bantex and Leitz, supplying files and folders in bulk to businesses, schools and government bodies nationwide. Explore the ranges below and request a quote, answered within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/display-books-clear-files/' => 'Display books and clear files, sometimes called presentation folders or clear book files, hold documents in transparent pockets so they can be read and flipped through without being removed. They are perfect for materials that are shown rather than stored, menus, portfolios, procedures, price lists on the shelf, tender submissions and reference sets that many people handle. The main choice is the number of pockets: display books come with fixed pocket counts, so estimate how many sheets you present and allow a little room to grow, while refillable binders with clear pockets suit collections that change often. Look at the pocket quality too, because thin pockets tear at the punch holes under frequent use, and a sturdy cover protects the contents and keeps the book looking professional in client-facing settings. For schools preparing lesson materials or offices assembling proposal packs, clear files keep everything neat, legible and protected from thumb marks and dust. OfficeLand stocks display books and clear files in various pocket capacities and colours, including options from Bantex, with delivery to offices and schools across Nigeria. Send us your requirements and we will return a quote within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/dividers-index/' => 'Dividers and index sets turn a thick file into something anyone can navigate, splitting binders and lever arch files into clearly marked sections so the right page is found in moments. This matters most in heavy registry and project files, where flicking through hundreds of loose sheets wastes time every single day. When choosing, start with the number of parts you need, from a handful of broad categories up to full A-Z index sets, and match the punching to your binder, whether two-ring, four-ring or multi-punched for lever arch use. Material makes a real difference to lifespan: card dividers are economical for lighter files, while laminated or polypropylene tabs resist bending and survive constant thumbing in a busy office. Reinforced punch holes are worth having wherever pages are turned all day. Consider printable or write-on tabs so sections can be labelled to match your own filing scheme. OfficeLand supplies dividers, subject dividers and index sets in a range of part counts and materials, including dependable options from Bantex and Leitz, delivered in bulk to offices, schools and government registries nationwide. Tell us your sizes and quantities for a quote within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/document-files-boxes/' => 'Document files and box files bridge the gap between a slim folder and a full archive box, giving active or semi-active paperwork a firm, self-contained home that stands on a shelf. Box files with a spring clip or ring mechanism keep loose documents secure yet accessible, while expanding document files with multiple pockets or a concertina design group related papers, receipts, correspondence or case notes, in one portable unit. When selecting, look at the spine width and capacity against the volume you file, and check the closure: a strong clip, elastic fastener or press-stud keeps contents from spilling when a file is carried or shelved on its side. Rigid board or polypropylene construction decides how well the file copes with repeated handling and Lagos humidity, with wipeable plastic the safer choice for long storage in damp conditions. A labelled spine lets a whole shelf be read at a glance. OfficeLand stocks box files and expanding document files in practical capacities and finishes, including options from Bantex, supplied to offices, schools and registries across Nigeria. Request a quote for bulk orders and we will reply within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/lever-arch-files/' => 'Lever arch files are the standard choice for bulky, long-lived records, and they are what most Nigerian registries reach for when a folder simply will not hold enough. The lever mechanism opens wide so sheets can be added or removed anywhere in the sequence without disturbing the rest, and a broad spine carries far more than a ring binder of the same footprint. When buying, match the spine width to your volume, and give priority to build quality: a strong metal lever, rigid board or polypropylene covers and reinforced edges are what separate a file that lasts years from one that collapses within months of daily use. Metal spine shoes and a thumb hole make shelving and pulling heavy files easier on the hands. For long-term storage in humid conditions, polypropylene-covered files resist moisture far better than plain board. Colour coding across departments speeds filing and retrieval, and ordering consistent sizes keeps cabinets uniform. OfficeLand stocks lever arch files from trusted brands including Bantex and Leitz, in a choice of sizes and colours, supplied in bulk to offices, schools and government bodies nationwide. Searching for lever arch files in Nigeria, request a quote answered within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/manila-folders/' => 'Manila folders are the simplest and most widely used filing item of all, the plain card folder that holds a single matter, client or case and slots into a drawer, suspension pocket or box. Their value is in volume and consistency, so the key decisions are weight and size. Heavier gsm card stands up to repeated handling in an active registry, while lighter card is economical for short-lived or overflow filing. Match the cut and size to your system, foolscap folders for most Nigerian offices, with square-cut folders sitting flat in boxes and suspension-compatible folders designed to drop into hanging pockets. Consider colours for coding by department, year or status, which makes large volumes of files far quicker to sort and retrieve. Because manila is absorbent, keep long-term files off damp floors and walls, as Nigeria\'s humidity will soften and stain card left in poor conditions. For schools, clinics and government registries that get through folders by the hundred, buying in bulk keeps stock uniform and costs predictable. OfficeLand supplies manila and square-cut folders in a range of weights, sizes and colours, delivered nationwide. Request a quote within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/report-clip-files/' => 'Report files and clip files are the quick, tidy way to present or hold a modest set of loose sheets without punching and filing them into a binder. A report file typically has a slide bar or fastener that grips the pages along one edge, giving a clean, bound look that suits proposals, reports, student assignments and documents passed between desks for review. Clip files and clipboards with a cover keep forms secure for use away from the desk, on a store count, a site visit or a school inspection. When choosing, consider how many sheets the mechanism holds, since slide bars and fasteners are designed for lighter volumes than a lever arch file, and look at the cover, a clear front shows the title page while a solid cover protects contents in transit. Durable polypropylene survives being carried about far better than thin card. For presentation in volume, matching colours and styles give a consistent, professional finish. OfficeLand stocks report files, clip files and fastener folders in various capacities and finishes, supplied to offices and schools across Nigeria. Send your quantities for a quote within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/ring-binders/' => 'Ring binders keep punched documents secure yet easy to reorder, making them the natural home for manuals, training packs, policy sets and any reference material that is updated as it grows. The first choice is the ring mechanism: two-ring binders are common for everyday A4 filing, while four-ring versions hold pages more firmly and resist tearing at the punch holes under frequent turning. Ring shape matters for capacity, round rings suit lighter contents, while D-shaped rings hold more sheets flat and keep them aligned. Match the ring size to your volume rather than overfilling, which strains the mechanism and splays pages. For presentation, look at covers with a clear outer pocket for a printed spine and front, useful for a shelf of shared manuals in an office or school. Sturdy covers and a smooth, well-aligned mechanism are what keep a binder working after heavy use. OfficeLand stocks ring binders in a range of ring counts, sizes and colours, including options from Bantex and Leitz, supplied in bulk to offices, schools and organisations nationwide. Request a quote answered within four working hours.',

    '/filing-storage/files-folders/suspension-files/' => 'Suspension files, also searched for as hanging files, hang from the rails inside a filing cabinet or a suspension frame so each file stands upright and slides smoothly for quick retrieval. They are the standard system for active drawer filing in offices and registries, and getting them right starts with matching the file to your cabinet, foolscap or A4, and checking the rail width so the hooks sit correctly. Look at the card weight and base style: a strong base, whether V-shaped or a flat-bottomed box file for thicker contents, decides how many sheets each pocket carries without sagging. Printable tabs and inserts let you label files clearly and keep an alphabetical or numerical sequence easy to scan. Pair suspension files with square-cut manila folders inside each pocket so individual matters can be lifted out and carried without disturbing the drawer. For humid Nigerian conditions, keep cabinets away from damp walls to protect the card over the long term. OfficeLand supplies suspension files, tabs and inserts, including options from Bantex and Leitz, in bulk to offices, schools and government registries nationwide, with suspension files available in Lagos and delivered countrywide. Request a quote within four working hours.',
